<Marketing
  title="Grossline — terms"
  description="The terms of the Grossline reporting service: what it is, the access it needs, how numbers are produced, fees, and liability."
  path="/terms"
>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Terms of service</div>
      <h1>The deal, in plain terms.</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 15 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose-section" style="padding-top:48px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The service</h2>
        <p>
          Grossline reports on your own commerce and advertising data. Each report is prepared for
          the brand it's addressed to. It is information to help you run your business — it is not
          financial, tax or investment advice, and you make your own decisions from it.
        </p>

        <h2>Access</h2>
        <p>
          You grant us read-only access to the platforms your engagement covers — your Shopify store
          and your Google and Meta ad accounts. We never write to your store or your ad accounts,
          and we can't spend your money. You can revoke our access at any time from inside those
          platforms.
        </p>

        <h2>How the numbers are produced</h2>
        <p>
          Figures are computed from the data the platforms give us. Platforms sometimes restate
          their own history — Meta revises recent days, for example — so a report reflects the data
          available when it was produced. What we mean by each term ("net sales", "a new customer",
          "what you kept") is written down and applied the same way every month.
        </p>

        <h2>The free first report</h2>
        <p>
          Your first month's report is free, with a call to go through it. There's no obligation to
          continue afterwards.
        </p>

        <h2>Fees and billing</h2>
        <p>
          Ongoing plans are a flat monthly fee based on your ad-spend band, billed quarterly in
          advance, with a one-time setup fee to connect everything and pull your history. There's no
          lock-in — the plans are on our <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> page.
        </p>

        <h2>Stopping</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop at any time by telling us. We revoke access, stop billing for future periods,
          and delete your data on request.
        </p>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          The service is provided as-is. To the maximum extent the law allows, our liability for any
          claim arising from the service is limited to the fees you paid for the month in which the
          claim arose. Nothing here limits any liability that can't be limited by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of India, and disputes fall to the courts of
          Ahmedabad, Gujarat.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms:
          <a href="mailto:hello@getgrossline.com">hello@getgrossline.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
